# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5, cuda
# `observe` in the Python model on a GPU (D[python-observe]): the file of
# `[output] observables` (D189) written by ObservablesReporter and the values
# of State.observables, against `mdir run` on the same model, byte for byte
# in the deterministic mode: a pair term, a term over bonds, and the walls of
# D189 on the dipeptide in water; an NBFIX written as a pair term on the
# mixture of pair-dispersion.test, whose columns take its tail and shift
# estimate (D209, D210; against their closed forms), also in NPT; runs in
# parts, a period of its own, a continuation from a checkpoint; the
# refusals; terms of the positions (D[python-external]); tunables in the
# same program, with dU/dl against gradient() (D230) and central differences.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_observe.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide %t GPU mdir %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double cutoff: 5 rows of 10 columns (pair, bonds, walls) equal to mdir run's file byte for byte, and the state's values to its rows
# CHECK: GPU Double shift: 5 rows of 10 columns
# CHECK: GPU Mixed cutoff: 5 rows of 10 columns
# CHECK: GPU Mixed shift: 5 rows of 10 columns (pair, bonds, walls) equal to mdir run's file byte for byte, and the state's values to its rows
# CHECK: parts: runs of 7 and 13 steps write the file of one run; a period of its own; backup; a late reporter
# CHECK: checkpoint: continued at step 10 with append, the file of one run
# CHECK: refusals: an unknown constant, a name twice
# CHECK: external terms: refusals; 1146 particles by index equal to the mask ':WAT'
# CHECK: GPU Double external terms: 1146 particles, the walls' energies 5035.071714 and 3389.462793 kcal/mol within
# CHECK-SAME: 10 steps: the energy file byte for byte and the positions, velocities, and forces of the checkpoint of mdir run to the bit
# CHECK: GPU Mixed external terms: 1146 particles
# CHECK-SAME: to the bit
# CHECK: GPU Double cutoff: the mixture's rows equal to mdir run's file byte for byte; the correction adds, as its closed forms, nbfix.energy -1.921376, nbfix.d_sig -43.801428, nbfix.d_eps -1.291884
# CHECK: GPU Double shift: the mixture's rows equal to mdir run's file byte for byte
# CHECK: GPU Mixed cutoff: the mixture's rows equal to mdir run's file byte for byte
# CHECK: GPU Mixed shift: the mixture's rows equal to mdir run's file byte for byte
# CHECK: GPU Double NPT: 5 rows equal to mdir run's file byte for byte
# CHECK: GPU Mixed NPT: 5 rows
# CHECK: GPU Double tunables: the columns follow an update, with its version in the row; an observed tunable of one entry: soft.d_l 13365.9{{[0-9]+}} kJ/mol/nm against gradient()
# CHECK-SAME: several entries refused
# CHECK: GPU Mixed tunables: the columns follow an update
# CHECK: python observe passed
